      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=-4R_{1}$ on $X?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{1}:=-4R_{1}$ means that we need to multiply the first row of the matrix by $-4.$\n\nMultiplying the $1$st row by $-4$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-3 & 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=-4R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-4\\cdot (-3) & -4\\cdot 2 & -4\\cdot (-2) & -4\\cdot (-3) \\\\ -3 & 5 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}12 & -8 & 8 & 12 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -8 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
